gui.brave.points.rule.content=1. Warrior points are part of the rules for the regular stage of ranked matches (get one star for each victory, lose one star for each loss), and meant to encourage gaining stars. \\n2. Players will get warrior points from ranked matches. \\n3. Warrior points gained = base points + points for performance in game + consecutive victory points + active confrontation points \\n① Base points: 3 points (0 point if there is AFK behavior) \\n② Points for performance in game: 3 points for gold medal and 2 points for silver medal, max 3 points \\n ③ Consecutive victory points: the more consecutive victories, the more points added. There is an upper limit \\n ④ Active confrontation points \\n(1) when the team's total rank is lower than the highest total ranked team by a certain amount\\n(2)There are players on your team that left\\n4. Rank protection: When a certain number of warrior points is achieved, rank protection sytem will automatically take effect. When player loses a match, warrior points will be consumed to protect stars. The points required to protect stars increase as the rank increases. \\n5. Bonus star gain: When warrior points reach the upper limit and the player wins another ranked match, they can consume the same amount warrior points needed for protection in the current rank in order to get an extra star.
